{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2U4ddCNVmPmnLvxVVo6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On upright phones the door is fixed: 阿檀 (including her reaching arm) and the whole mirror are now in frame, with the face clear. The mirror shows the face going from 3 painted layers, to 1 layer after 让她擦, to clean once you discard a card. `check_engine` passes, `index.packed.html` is rebuilt, and I opened the packed file on the local server to confirm the new shot is used.\n\n**What I changed** (all in `原型/v1.7/index.html`, upright phones only):\n- **Door shot:** a new `VIEWS.doorP` view, lower and flatter than the morning shot, so it reads as \"just came in the door\" rather than looking down at the morning table. The darker door lighting is unchanged. 阿檀 is on the left, the mirror on the right.\n- **Night shot (the optional extra):** the same fix in a new `VIEWS.nightP`. At night the mirror used to be half out of frame; it's now complete.\n- **Narrower phones:** these upright-only shots pull back in proportion on phones narrower than 390×844, such as 360×800, so the mirror doesn't touch the edge. 390×844 and 375×812 are unaffected.\n- **Towel animation:** the towel is attached to the camera, and on a narrow screen it covered the whole picture for a moment. That was already true before this change; it was just more noticeable with the new shot. I narrowed it on upright phones only, so it now looks like a cloth wiping from left to right.\n\nDesktop and phone landscape still use the original shots and look the same as before. The morning fix from last round hasn't regressed.\n\n**Trade-off:** fitting both 阿檀 and the whole mirror into a narrow screen means pulling back. The mirror is about 120px wide at 390, similar to the morning shot. You can see the face and how much paint is left, but it isn't a close-up. A bigger mirror would mean cutting 阿檀 out of the frame, which the brief asks me not to do.\n\n**Not fixed:**\n- In phone landscape (844×390), the water board in the top right already covers part of the mirror at the door. The brief said not to touch landscape this round, so it's worth a separate fix later.\n- I only tested in a browser simulator (390, 375 and 360 wide, plus a WeChat-sized 390×680), not on a real phone.\n\nScreenshots are in `設計/美術/feedback_v17/qa_mobile_door/`: before and after, mirror close-ups across the wipe, three towel frames, desktop, landscape, night and the packed version. Write-ups are in `設計/美術/V17_DOOR_MIRROR_PROGRESS.md` and `V17_DOOR_MIRROR_RESULT.md`. As the brief asked, nothing has been committed or pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2770,"cache_read_input_tokens":212671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2770},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14631641-e1b7-4e19-b3b7-9c4cd1155a1e","uuid":"3f64a060-e697-4c9e-afe6-5b959ec2325d","timestamp":"2026-11-14T07:59:59.151Z","request_id":"req_011Ch2U4dAufEzLdobuGmY1n"}
